# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `make sanitize`
#
# links/rdn_link_vme.c models two CPUs sharing memory across a VME
# backplane. There are no atomic read-modify-write cycles across VME, so
# the ring is synchronised with ordered plain stores and hardware barriers
# (PowerPC "sync"): data words, barrier, index word. ThreadSanitizer only
# models locks and atomics, so it reports these deliberate accesses. The
# ring's ordering and restart behaviour are verified functionally by
# tests/test_vme_ring.c (20000-frame threaded ordering test, restart tests).
#
# Nothing else is suppressed: the runtime itself must be TSan-clean.
race:rdn_link_vme.c
